  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe makes 8 msemen and requires 20 minutes to prepare, 30 minutes of resting time and 25 minutes of cooking. The rest is essential for developing the gluten and making the dough pliable enough to stretch thin without tearing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: The folding technique is what creates the layers in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "msemen-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "msemen"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Each fold traps a thin layer of fat between the dough, which puffs and separates during cooking. Work on an oiled surface rather than a floured one to keep the dough supple."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
