      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Combine the flour, salt, sugar and black pepper in a large bowl. Gradually add the warm water, mixing until a soft, smooth dough forms. Knead for 8-10 minutes until the dough is elastic and no longer sticky."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Divide the dough into 8 equal pieces using digital scales for consistency. Roll each piece into a smooth ball. Cover with a clean cloth and rest for 30 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix the softened butter with 2 tbsp vegetable oil to make a spreadable paste. Oil your work surface lightly with the remaining vegetable oil."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Take one dough ball and flatten it on the oiled surface. Stretch and roll it out as thinly as possible, almost translucent. Spread a thin layer of the butter paste over the surface and scatter over a few sesame seeds."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fold the left third of the dough over the centre, then fold the right third on top. You will have a long rectangle. Fold the top third down and the bottom third up to make a small square. Set aside and repeat with the remaining balls."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Using your fingertips or a rolling pin, gently press each square out to approximately 15cm across. Do not overwork the dough at this stage or the layers will merge."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat a griddle pan over medium heat. Cook the msemen in batches for 3-4 minutes per side until golden brown with darker patches. They should feel dry and crisp on the outside and layered inside. Serve immediately with honey and butter, or alongside savoury dishes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "question": "The dough tears when stretched"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The dough needs more rest. Cover it again and leave for another 15 minutes. Under-rested dough is tight and resistant. Make sure your work surface is well oiled rather than floured, as flour makes the dough stiffen further."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "question": "The msemen have no visible layers"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Layers come from the fat between the folds. Make sure each sheet of stretched dough is well covered with the butter and oil paste before folding. Use enough fat to feel the surface is slick. Too little fat and the layers fuse together during cooking."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "question": "The msemen are burning on the outside before cooking through"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Reduce the heat to medium-low. Msemen need a moderate, steady heat to cook through to the centre. If the pan is too hot the outside chars before the inside warms. A cast-iron griddle or heavy frying pan holds heat more evenly than a thin pan."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Msemen are square flatbreads eaten across Morocco for breakfast. They are served with honey, argan oil, or jam. Street vendors sell them hot from griddles in the morning. The folding technique creates the layers. They cool down quickly, so eat them straight from the pan."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
